WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.054
was now on her own adventure.

2
00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:21.638
In the papyrus workshop, groups of men were making different things.

3
00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:25.761
Mandy saw a young boy make a ball like Akhom’s.

4
00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:29.024
Another person worked on a pair of sandals.

5
00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:34.113
“These reeds are for making paper,” the friendly man explained.

6
00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:37.174
He took a long reed from his bundle.

7
00:00:37.194 --> 00:00:40.295
“First you cut the reeds to make them shorter.

8
00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:43.356
Then you strip off the green skin.”

9
00:00:44.616 --> 00:00:46.797
The inside of the papyrus was white.

10
00:00:47.957 --> 00:00:50.878
The man used a knife to cut it into thin sheets.

11
00:00:52.238 --> 00:00:54.499
“You can do this part,” he said to Mandy.

12
00:00:54.519 --> 00:00:58.940
“Just put these sheets on this block,” he explained.

13
00:01:00.008 --> 00:01:03.209
Mandy sat down in front of the block.

14
00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.751
“Cover the papyrus with this cloth,” he continued.

15
00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:10.953
He gave Mandy a hammer.

16
00:01:10.973 --> 00:01:13.594
“Now beat the cloth evenly.”

17
00:01:14.955 --> 00:01:16.935
She gently hit the papyrus sheets.

18
00:01:16.955 --> 00:01:21.377
“This is amazing,” she exclaimed.

19
00:01:23.618 --> 00:01:27.400
Nodding, the man said, “Papyrus is a gift from the gods.”

20
00:01:28.892 --> 00:01:30.113
She lifted the cloth.

21
00:01:31.374 --> 00:01:33.736
The papyrus still felt thick and rough.

22
00:01:33.756 --> 00:01:40.441
“After the papyrus dries,” the man explained, “we will use this to make the surface smoother.”

23
00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:44.964
He picked up a shiny stone.

24
00:01:44.984 --> 00:01:51.589
“It’s time to go, Issa,” said another man, motioning to his friend.

25
00:01:51.609 --> 00:01:54.511
“Where are you going?”

26
00:01:55.171 --> 00:01:55.972
Mandy asked.

27
00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.681
“We must take the papyrus rope to the pyramid,” Issa replied.

28
00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.502
He pointed to coils of thick rope.

29
00:02:04.402 --> 00:02:07.683
Mandy had almost forgotten her brother and the glowing pyramid.

30
00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:09.984
“Can I come with you?”

31
00:02:10.564 --> 00:02:11.704
she asked her new friend.

32
00:02:12.744 --> 00:02:16.506
Shaking his head, Issa said, “That is no place for a young girl.

33
00:02:17.366 --> 00:02:18.446
You shouldn’t even be here.”

34
00:02:18.466 --> 00:02:23.127
“I promise not to get in the way,” she begged.

35
00:02:24.108 --> 00:02:24.908
Issa gave in.

36
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.321
“But you must stay in the boat,” he warned.

37
00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.663
Suddenly Mandy missed Vinnie.

38
00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:35.824
"Come on, Vinnie," she said in her mind.

39
00:02:35.844 --> 00:02:40.026
"The glowing pyramid is where we both want to go."

40
00:02:41.086 --> 00:02:43.868
She hoped her brother was thinking the same thing.

41
00:02:45.388 --> 00:02:48.890
Meanwhile, Vinnie and Akhom walked back to the market.

42
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.631
“I don’t see her anywhere!”

43
00:02:53.352 --> 00:02:54.032
cried Vinnie.

44
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.620
“Where would she go?”

45
00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.001
asked Akhom.

46
00:02:59.281 --> 00:03:00.601
Vinnie thought for a moment.

47
00:03:00.621 --> 00:03:04.022
“Wait!” He pulled out the photograph.

48
00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:07.143
The pyramid was now glowing blue.

49
00:03:07.163 --> 00:03:10.724
“Great Amon-Ra!”

50
00:03:11.164 --> 00:03:13.305
Akhom shouted, when he saw the photo.

51
00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:16.666
“Don’t worry,” comforted Vinnie.

52
00:03:16.686 --> 00:03:18.566
“It’s just a photo.”

53
00:03:18.586 --> 00:03:20.827
“A what?”

54
00:03:21.407 --> 00:03:22.867
Akhom opened one eye.

55
00:03:22.887 --> 00:03:25.544
“Never mind,” said Vinnie.

56
00:03:25.564 --> 00:03:28.466
“I think Mandy may be going there.”

57
00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:31.047
He pointed to the pyramid.

58
00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.247
“Do you know where this is?”

59
00:03:34.448 --> 00:03:37.049
Akhom cautiously studied the picture and shuddered.

60
00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.510
“Yes, it is the Pharaoh’s tomb along the Nile.”

61
00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.751
“Can you take me there?”

62
00:03:43.371 --> 00:03:44.032
asked Vinnie.

63
00:03:45.192 --> 00:03:46.473
Akhom did not answer.

64
00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:52.015
“Please, Akhom, I must find my sister,” begged Vinnie.

65
00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:54.536
Akhom finally agreed.

66
00:03:55.705 --> 00:03:58.782
“But we must be very careful because it is forbidden.”
